        "iid": "4230",
        "title": "fix(govern): read the fallback sync job's settings as launchd and systemd do [4 of 6]",
        "webUrl": "https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4230",
        "state": "opened",
        "draft": false,
        "description": "**Part 4 of 6.** Review and merge in order, starting with part 1 (https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4227). The full list is under **Where this sits**.\n\n## Description\n\nMakes the fallback periodic sync job carry `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, and makes glab read an installed job the way launchd and systemd do.\n\n- `fallbacksync.Job` gets `ClaudeConfigDir`. It is written as `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` in the launchd plist `EnvironmentVariables`, or as a systemd `Environment=` line.\n- `Units` refuses any job value with a control character (`InvalidJobError`) before anything changes.\n- `Install` writes every unit to a temp file before it renames any into place, so a failed write leaves the previous job's files as they were.\n- When a job fails to load, systemd gets `disable --now` and `daemon-reload`, and launchd gets `launchctl print`. It returns `RemovedError{MayStillRun}` when glab could not confirm the old job is unloaded.\n- `InstalledBinary` on systemd reads the first `ExecStart=` after drop-ins. This is the new `systemd.go` parser (drop-in dirs, quoting, specifiers). macOS is unchanged.\n- `InstalledClaudeConfigDir` is new. It reads the job's `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` from the plist, from `systemctl --user show` when an executor is given, or else from the service and its drop-ins. It returns an error for `EnvironmentFile=`, `UnsetEnvironment=`, `PassEnvironment=` and a relative value. Its caller arrives in part 6.\n- `setup.go`, two small hunks: `installFallbackSync` passes the cleaned `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` into the job, and the install error now has three cases (old job removed and may still run, old job removed, old job unchanged).\n\n### Why `systemd.go` is not a separate MR\n\nYou asked for the launchd and systemd parsing to be separate. Its functions are all unexported and only `fallbacksync.go` calls them, so on its own it would fail the `unused` linter. It travels with `fallbacksync.go` in this MR.\n\nThe two `setup.go` hunks are here for two reasons. Unloading a job that failed to load would otherwise break `TestRunSetup_FallbackSyncFailureIsAWarning` (it expects one `systemctl` call, and now there are three). And passing `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` makes `Job.ClaudeConfigDir` used code. Part 6 replaces `setup.go` and `setup_test.go` with the final versions.\n\n### Where this sits\n\nPart 4 of 6 in the split of https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4196. Base branch is `andrew-jung/630020-split-3-claude-config-dir` (https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4229). It can merge now.\n\n1. https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4227: redact tokens in debug dumps\n2. https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4228: cmdtest isolation\n3. https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4229: `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`\n4. This MR: fallback job settings\n5. https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4231: `agentsession` and `govern session` (Draft)\n6. https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4196: `setup --mcp` (Draft)\n\nIt needs part 2 (`fallbacksync/main_test.go`). It uses nothing from part 3. It sits after part 3 so the two can merge back to back: part 3 makes setup write hooks under `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, and this MR makes the job look there too.\n\n## Related Issues\n\nRelated to https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab/-/issues/630020\n\n## How has this been tested?\n\n```shell\ngo test ./internal/commands/govern/...\n```\n\nAlso run: `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `GOOS=windows go build ./...` and `make gen-docs` (no diff).\n\nTo try it on Linux: set `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` to an absolute path, run `glab govern setup`, and check that `systemctl --user show` for the job lists `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` in its environment.",
